## Code Style & Conventions

### TypeScript
- Use TypeScript for all files
- Define types in `types.ts` for shared interfaces and enums
- Use interfaces for component props: `interface ComponentProps { ... }`
- Use explicit return types for functions when beneficial: `React.FC<Props>` or explicit return types
- Use `type` aliases for union types: `type Page = 'home' | 'donate' | 'history' | 'admin' | 'login'`
- Prefer `Omit<>` utility type when creating partial types: `Omit<DonationItem, 'id' | 'status' | 'submittedAt'>`

### React Components
- Use functional components exclusively
- Use React hooks (`useState`, `useContext`, `useEffect`, etc.)
- Components should be exported as default: `export default ComponentName`
- Use `React.FC<Props>` type annotation for components
- Define props interfaces above the component
- Extract reusable sub-components within the same file when appropriate
- Use descriptive component and prop names

### Naming Conventions
- **Components**: PascalCase (e.g., `DonationForm`, `Header`)
- **Files**: PascalCase for components/pages (e.g., `DonationForm.tsx`, `HomePage.tsx`)
- **Functions/Variables**: camelCase (e.g., `handleSubmit`, `donationService`)
- **Types/Interfaces**: PascalCase (e.g., `DonationItem`, `User`)
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants, camelCase for mock data (e.g., `MOCK_DONOR_USER`)

### Context & State Management
- Use React Context API for global state (authentication, user data)
- Export context provider component (e.g., `AuthProvider`)
- Export custom hook for accessing context (e.g., `useAuth()`)
- Custom hooks should throw error if used outside provider
- Context files should be in `context/` directory

### Service Layer
- Service functions should be async and return Promises
- Use descriptive function names: `getDonations`, `addDonation`, `updateDonationStatus`, `getMatches`, `createRequest`, etc.
- Service functions should handle errors and throw appropriate errors
- Simulate API delays with `setTimeout` or `delay()` helper when using mock data
- Service files should be in `services/` directory and export functions
- **Image Service** (`imageService.ts`): Handles image compression (max 500KB), resizing (max 1920x1080), validation (type, size), supports multiple images (up to 5)
- **Export Service** (`exportService.ts`): Handles CSV/JSON/PDF exports for donations, donor activity reports, statistics
- **Matching Service** (`matchingService.ts`): Handles donation-request matching with scoring algorithm (category, quantity, location, urgency weights)
- **Master Data Service** (`masterDataService.ts`): Manages categories, status types, urgency levels, roles & permissions, matching algorithm configuration
- **User Management Service** (`userManagementService.ts`): Handles user CRUD, role assignment, account status, verification, activity tracking

### Styling (TailwindCSS)
- Use TailwindCSS utility classes exclusively
- Primary brand color: `teal-500` / `teal-600` / `teal-700`
- Use responsive prefixes: `md:`, `sm:`, `lg:`
- Mobile-first approach: base styles for mobile, add `md:` and up for larger screens
- Common patterns:
  - Buttons: `bg-teal-500 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-md hover:bg-teal-600 transition`
  - Cards: `bg-white rounded-lg shadow-lg p-6`
  - Forms: `border border-gray-300 rounded-md focus:ring-teal-500 focus:border-teal-500`
- Use semantic spacing utilities: `space-y-6`, `gap-4`, `mb-8`
- Use flex/grid utilities for layouts

### Routing & Navigation
- Use local state in `App.tsx` for page routing (not a router library)
- Page types: `'home' | 'donate' | 'history' | 'admin' | 'login' | 'profile' | 'impact' | 'donor-management' | 'recipient-registration' | 'request-items' | 'matching' | 'master-data' | 'user-management'`
- Implement navigation guards: check auth before allowing access to protected pages
- Redirect unauthenticated users to login page when accessing protected routes
- Role-based routing: admin-only pages (`admin`, `donor-management`, `matching`, `master-data`, `user-management`), recipient-only pages (`request-items`)
- Profile page routing: route to `DonorProfile` for donors, `RecipientProfile` for recipients based on user role(s)
- Pass `onNavigate` callback to pages/components that need navigation
- Multi-role users: check `user.roles` array or `user.role` for access control (e.g., `user.role === 'admin' || user.roles?.includes('recipient')`)

### Error Handling
- Use try/catch blocks for async operations
- Display user-friendly error messages in UI
- Set error state for form validation errors
- Show error messages using TailwindCSS styled divs: `bg-red-100 text-red-800 rounded-md`

### Loading States
- Use loading states for async operations: `'idle' | 'loading' | 'success' | 'error'`
- Show loading spinners during async operations
- Use `loading` boolean from context for auth operations
- Disable buttons during loading: `disabled={status === 'loading'}`

### Form Handling
- Use controlled components with `useState`
- Validate required fields before submission
- Show validation errors clearly
- Reset forms after successful submission
- Use proper input types: `text`, `tel`, `number`, `textarea`, `file`, `email`, `date`
- **Image Upload**: Support multiple images (up to 5), validate file type and size, use `imageService.ts` for compression/resizing
- **Multi-step Forms**: Use step-by-step progress indicators (e.g., RecipientRegistration has 3 steps)
- **Password Strength**: Show visual password strength indicator with color coding
- **Email Validation**: Real-time email availability checking with debouncing
- **File Upload**: Handle file validation, preview, compression before submission

### Component Patterns
- **Page Components**: Located in `pages/`, handle routing and page-level logic
- **Reusable Components**: Located in `components/`, should be generic and reusable
- **Service Functions**: Pure functions, no side effects except data operations
- **Context Providers**: Wrap app at root level in `App.tsx`

## File Organization
- Group related files in directories (`components/`, `pages/`, `services/`, `context/`)
- Each component/page should be in its own file
- Shared types in `types.ts` at root
- Export only what's needed from each file

## Best Practices
1. **Component Composition**: Break down complex components into smaller, focused components
2. **Type Safety**: Use TypeScript strictly, avoid `any` type
3. **Immutability**: Don't mutate state directly, use setState functions
4. **Accessibility**: Use semantic HTML, proper labels for form inputs
5. **Responsive Design**: Always consider mobile, tablet, and desktop views
6. **Code Reusability**: Extract common logic into hooks or utilities
7. **Error Boundaries**: Consider error boundaries for production apps
8. **Performance**: Use proper React patterns (avoid unnecessary re-renders)

## Common Patterns

### Component with Props
```typescript
interface ComponentProps {
    onNavigate: (page: Page) => void;
    currentPage: Page;
}

const Component: React.FC<ComponentProps> = ({ onNavigate, currentPage }) => {
    // component logic
};
```

### Using Context
```typescript
const { user, loading, login, logout } = useAuth();
```

### Service Call Pattern
```typescript
const [status, setStatus] = useState<'idle' | 'loading' | 'success' | 'error'>('idle');
try {
    setStatus('loading');
    await serviceFunction();
    setStatus('success');
} catch (err) {
    setStatus('error');
}
```

### Button with Loading State
```typescript
<button
    disabled={status === 'loading'}
    className="... disabled:bg-teal-300 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
>
    {status === 'loading' ? 'Loading...' : 'Submit'}
</button>
```

### Image Upload Pattern
```typescript
import { compressImage, validateImage } from '../services/imageService';

const handleImageUpload = async (files: FileList) => {
    const validImages = await Promise.all(
        Array.from(files).map(async (file) => {
            if (!validateImage(file)) throw new Error('Invalid image');
            return await compressImage(file);
        })
    );
    // Use compressed images
};
```

### Role-based Rendering
```typescript
const { user } = useAuth();

// Check for single role
{user.role === 'admin' && <AdminPanel />}

// Check for multiple roles
{(user.role === 'recipient' || user.roles?.includes('recipient')) && <RequestButton />}

// Check for both roles
{user.roles?.includes('donor') && user.roles?.includes('recipient') && <BothRolesView />}
```

### Matching Service Pattern
```typescript
import { getMatchingSuggestions, confirmMatch } from '../services/matchingService';

const [matches, setMatches] = useState<Match[]>([]);
const suggestions = await getMatchingSuggestions(donationId);
// Process matching suggestions with scores (0-100)
```

### Master Data Service Pattern
```typescript
import { getCategories, getStatusTypes, getRoles } from '../services/masterDataService';

const categories = await getCategories();
const statusTypes = await getStatusTypes();
const roles = await getRoles();
// Use master data for dropdowns, filters, etc.
```

## User Roles & Permissions

### User Roles
- **Donor**: Can donate items, view donation history, achievements, goals, leaderboard
- **Recipient**: Can create item requests, view recipient profile, receive donations
- **Admin**: Full access to admin dashboard, user management, donor management, matching, master data management
- **Multi-role**: Users can have multiple roles (e.g., both donor and recipient) via `roles` array in User interface

### Role-based Access Control
- Check `user.role === 'admin'` for admin-only features
- Check `user.role === 'recipient' || user.roles?.includes('recipient')` for recipient features
- Check `user.role === 'donor' || user.roles?.includes('donor')` for donor features
- Master Data Management provides granular role-based permissions via Roles & Permissions system
- User Management System handles role assignment and management

## Key Features & Systems

### Master Data Management
- **Categories**: Donation and request categories with hierarchy, icons, colors, custom fields, visibility settings
- **Status Types**: Unified status configuration (donation, request, delivery, verification, matching statuses)
- **Urgency Levels**: Priority/urgency levels (High/Urgent, Medium, Low) with scoring weights
- **Roles & Permissions**: System roles with granular permissions matrix (read, write, delete, approve, manage, view, export)
- **Matching Algorithm Configuration**: Matching score weights (category, quantity, location, urgency, request age)

### User Management System
- Unified user administration (donors, recipients, admins, moderators)
- User CRUD operations, role assignment, account status management
- Account verification workflow (pending, verified, rejected)
- User activity tracking (login history, activity timeline)
- User tags, communication history, bulk operations

### Matching System
- Automatic matching suggestions with scoring algorithm (0-100 score)
- Manual matching interface for admins
- Batch matching support (one donation to multiple recipients or vice versa)
- Partial fulfillment support (split donations)
- Match confirmation workflow (confirm, reject, fulfill, cancel)

### Donation Features
- Multi-image upload (up to 5 images per donation)
- Image compression (max 500KB) and resizing (max 1920x1080)
- Admin notes (private notes visible only to admins)
- Action history tracking (status changes, quantity updates)
- Donation details modal with image gallery, status timeline, inline editing

### Request System (Recipients)
- Create item requests with category, quantity, description, urgency level
- Multiple active requests per recipient
- Request status tracking (pending approval, approved, matched, fulfilled, cancelled, expired)
- Auto-expiry for old requests (configurable, default 90 days)
- Image upload support for requests

### Donor Profile Features
- Personal donation statistics (total donations, items delivered, people helped)
- Achievement badges/milestones (9 achievements with rarity levels: common, rare, epic, legendary)
- Donation goals with progress tracking (items, donations, categories)
- Donation trends chart (last 6 months)
- Favorite categories display (top 3 most donated categories)

### Recipient Profile Features
- Personal statistics dashboard (items received, requests submitted, fulfilled requests)
- Active requests overview with status badges
- Request history timeline with visual status tracking
- Profile customization (bio, family info, preferences)
- Communication preferences, notification settings
- Profile completeness indicator

### Impact & Engagement
- **Impact Stories**: Before/after photos, testimonials, impact metrics, featured stories
- **Leaderboard**: Top donors by items/quantity, monthly/all-time leaderboards, privacy controls
- **Homepage Stats**: Animated statistics cards with scroll-triggered animations

## Notes
- This is a two-way donation management platform - always consider both donor and recipient experiences
- Mock data is currently used in services - ready to be replaced with real API calls
- Authentication is currently mock-based - ready for real auth integration
- The app uses teal as the primary brand color - maintain consistency
- All pages should be responsive and mobile-friendly
- Users can have multiple roles (check `user.roles` array)
- Image handling uses `imageService.ts` for compression and resizing
- Export functionality uses `exportService.ts` for CSV/JSON/PDF exports
- Master Data Management is the central configuration system for categories, statuses, roles, etc.

## Development Guidelines
- Always test components on different screen sizes
- Ensure proper TypeScript typing throughout
- Maintain consistent code style and formatting
- Add proper error handling for all async operations
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Follow React best practices (hooks rules, dependency arrays, etc.)
- **Image Handling**: Always use `imageService.ts` for image compression and validation
- **Role Checks**: Always check both `user.role` and `user.roles` array for multi-role support
- **Master Data**: Use master data services for categories, statuses, roles instead of hardcoding
- **Export**: Use `exportService.ts` for all export functionality (CSV, JSON, PDF)
- **Matching**: Use `matchingService.ts` for all donation-request matching logic
- **Admin Notes**: Use `AdminNote` interface from `types.ts` for admin notes on donations
- **Status Management**: Use Master Data status types instead of hardcoding status values
- **User Management**: Use `userManagementService.ts` for all user CRUD and management operations

